<Base title="The events" current="/en/events/" lang="en" alt="/evenements/">
  <p class="eyebrow">The events</p>
  <h1>Earthdance, Sundari, Tatanka and the others</h1>
  <p class="lede">Five Earthdances, three Tatankas, a Sundari, a Reggae Bash, the very first Timeless, solstices, full moons, a self-managed camp, ceremonies. Everything the page and the websites announced, in order.</p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Earthdance, the global dance for peace</h2>
    <p>Earthdance is a synchronized festival, "in 60 countries and more than 200 places around the world", around the International Day of Peace, with a prayer for peace played at the same moment everywhere. Saint-Fortunat hosted one as early as 2007 and 2008; the Donjon, then L'AgorA, took it up every fall from 2010 to 2014, becoming an official Earthdance venue and, in 2013, a "peace-building organization" recognized by Earthdance Global. "For a last year presented at l'AgorA, we invite you to come and express, in your own way, according to your inspirations, what peace in the world means to you."</p>
  </div>

  <ul class="events">
    {events.map(([d, title, text]) => (
      <li><span>{d}</span><div><strong>{title}</strong>{text && <> — {text}</>}</div></li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2 class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:2.5rem">The posters</h2>
  <div class="gallery">
    {affiches.map(([file, caption, cls]) => (
      <figure class={cls}><img src={`/img/${file}`} alt={caption} loading="lazy" /><figcaption>{caption}</figcaption></figure>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 class="eyebrow">Party nights</h2>
  <div class="gallery">
    {photos.map(([file, caption, cls]) => (
      <figure class={cls}><img src={`/img/${file}`} alt={caption} loading="lazy" /><figcaption>{caption}</figcaption></figure>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>The site rules, 2013</h2>
    <p>The text handed to the festival-goers of Tatanka and Earthdance 2013 began with a clarification: "When you visit the Agora, you are entering the home and workplace of several people who wish to share with you the vision of a creative world in harmony with nature." Then came the rules, in both languages:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>"Respect our agricultural spaces, they are sacred to us!!"</li>
      <li>"When you go through the village of St-Fortunat, please don't shout!"</li>
      <li>No parking on route 263: "you will get a $60 ticket from the police, ask the parking attendant for a spot".</li>
      <li>"Use ONLY THE 8 DRY TOILETS and above all do not go to the other side of route 263, given the number of complaints we have received."</li>
      <li>"The MAIN's music will be inside the BUNKER from midnight to 8 AM, a CHILL stage will be outside at night and several activities in the forest are planned."</li>
      <li>Strictly no smoking in the barn; no glass bottles, "please bring cans"; sorting of waste.</li>
      <li>"Come prepared with your food, your sleeping bag, warm clothes, a towel, a flashlight, a raincoat…"</li>
      <li>"PLEASE keep your cigarette butts to dispose of them in the fire… because it can take weeks to pick up all the butts you see on the ground by the hundreds."</li>
      <li>"Fires will only be allowed in designated areas. NO fires will be tolerated in the spruce plantations. The ground can catch fire at any moment."</li>
    </ul>
    <p>"Thank you for your participation, understanding and vigilance!!"</p>
    <h2>The Earthdance 2011 line-up</h2>
    <p>From Friday evening to Sunday afternoon, almost non-stop, with two "let's take a walk on the wild side" breaks: DJ Shalom, DJ YvY, DJane Fatima, DJ MadChris, DJ Psychotik, Celktik and Kinematik, DJ Audiophil, DJ Tegavs, DJ Naaz, DJ Risa, DJ Prana Papa, Eric Mandala live, DJ Om Shanti, DJane Lemon Balm, DJ Karmapa, DJ Jeff MKUltra, DJ Rikam, DJ Decode, Longstocking &amp; Boom Tara, DJ Magnetic Phil, DJ Spo_Onani, DJ Glitch, and to close, "A gore A". Styles announced: world psy, tek-trance, tribal house, dubstep, full on, psytrance, cumbia, world music, goa, progressive, minimal techno.</p>

    <h2 id="sundari-2011">The Sundari 2011 programme</h2>
    <p>The festival's page on ledonjon.ca, captured by the Wayback Machine on May 18, 2011, announced a "100% ambient festival": "The next 3-4-5th of June 2011… We will have the honor to receive on this Appalachian mountain Adham Shaikh and Uwe Neumann, with other accompanying musicians, in this unique adventure proper to enchantment. Attention, hold on the magic carpet!" And, throughout the festival, "a welcoming place for kids and grown-ups", activities in nature "for your little sailors", camping "with possible electrical hook-ups", two lakes and a river for swimming, a mountain and its trail, free spring water, food stands, healing stands, "enchanting, breathtaking scenery".</p>
    <details>
      <summary>The live acts, the DJs, the workshops, the booths and the tickets</summary>
      <p><strong>Live</strong> — Dreamtree Project (Nelson, B.C. / Val-Morin), "the Indian dub fusion project of Juno nominee Adham Shaikh and Uwe Neumann"; Adham Shaikh (Nelson); Apadooraï (Montreal), "kind of an aboriginal rebel child… a symbiosis between a duo of didgeridoo freaks"; Lutin des Bois (Paris), founder of Secret Vibes; FreeWorm (Montreal), "the sound environmentalist" who produces "electro-organic"; Xnorophis (Montreal), "organic marginal music", with "a new tribal dub set for Sundari"; Tetsuo Tek (Similkameen Valley, B.C.), "a fairly dark dubstep set that will surprise you"; Rob-Vector (Boston), "a fan of Dreamtree Project, he's coming all the way to us"; Monokongo (Montreal), "a prog tribal set".</p>
      <p><strong>DJs</strong> — Dub Style Selectah live vs Sabi Non Stop (Montreal), dub; Rikam vs Mat THC (Montreal), of Tech Safari and the Éclipse festival, "an ambient psychedelic vs downtempo set, a special for the occasion"; Seb vs Kiran (Montreal), Mandala sound &amp; vision, "an ethno ambient set à la Interchill"; Bendala (Montreal), "worldbeat peace &amp; love"; Psyberth (Montreal), psychill "with organic, tribal and melodic sounds"; Longstocking vs Aquarius (Montreal); Solar Prophecy (Sherbrooke); YvY (Sherbrooke), "a vibratory unification of love in a small point in the universe that is the Earth"; Lunar Groove (Montreal), chill-out; Psyrenity (Montreal), tribal psychill; Deception (Montreal), "a mix of goa and prog full of surprises"; SpoOnani (Quebec City), chill-out drum'n'bass; Prana Papa (Quebec City), "from chaïchill to psyworld"; Zen (Inverness), of Altar Records, "active since 1995 in the underground trance and psychedelic ambient scene"; Andreï K (Montreal); Semira (Quebec City), "groovy earth chill"; Alakazoo (Saint-Fortunat), Psy Bûcheron Prod, "a psy dub downtempo set at 70 bpm"; Sinaë (Montreal); Zven (Montreal), psychedelic ambient.</p>
      <p><strong>The decor</strong> — Psychedelic Sanctuary Creations (Montreal), Cosmo (Peterborough), "Cosmic SpaceCrafts", and the Lune Noire (Saint-Fortunat).</p>
      <p><strong>The workshops</strong> — sacred geometry, by Cosmo; hula hoop, "the principles and foundations of hooping", by Valérie Hanson; "Dreadlocks 101, myths and facts", by Alle Sundari; Break Dance Ballet, with Ketty and Alle, "two of the most extreme opposites of dance… Eat, breathe, sleep, dance".</p>
      <p><strong>The booths</strong> — La Moustache Verte, wheatgrass juice; L'Arbre à Palabre, tea room; TrancePlants, shamanic and medicinal plants; Le Baril Roulant, craft beers; Resto chez Mmmm, soups, salads, sandwiches; Le Donjon, coffee and information; Zenergica, massages; a healing area; DJ Zen, CD sales.</p>
      <p><strong>The tickets</strong> — $35 "for the first 15 tickets bought online via PayPal", $40 until February 28, $50 until June 3, $60 at the door; on sale at Psychonaut in Montreal, at the Arbre à Palabre in Sherbrooke, at Exo in Quebec City, at Chanvre du Nord in Saint-Jérôme and at Shanti Baba in Toronto. The lodges of the indoor campground, "includes electricity and running water", were reserved through PayPal. Signed: "For universal love… which will allow real change. The team of the Donjon, grandeur nature!"</p>
    </details>
    <p>A "Sundari Transport" page organized the shuttle: departure from the Sherbrooke metro station in Montreal, "meeting point corner of Square Saint-Louis and St-Denis", Friday June 3 at noon (arrival in Saint-Fortunat at 2:30 pm) or at 8 pm (arrival at 10:30 pm, "full"), return on Sunday; $30 round trip, "limited seats, reserve soon when purchasing your festival ticket".</p>

    <h2 id="tatanka-2013">The Tatanka 2013 programme</h2>
    <p>In June 2013, the address ledonjon.ca led straight to the festival's page, "painted" by Tekout, Lune Noire and Six Feet High: "Tatanka is back in force in 2013 for its second edition!" Three outdoor stages, "more than 50 DJs of international calibre", street and circus artists, VJs, belly dancers, workshops, silly games, free camping, a restaurant on site and a "Relaxation Lounge area" with massages, rugs, cushions and shishas. The styles announced: techno, psy/prog, electroswing/balkan, dubstep, techouse/electro, chill/psybient, slam poets, d&amp;b/jungle, dub/psydub, worldbeat, breakbeat, "scratchers on turntables". Tickets at $25 in March ("online only, sold out"), $35 in April, $45 in May, $55 in June, $70 at the door. The original page, with its photos, is preserved in the <a href="/archives/ledonjon-ca-wayback/">archives</a>.</p>
    <details>
      <summary>The live acts, the DJs, the visuals and the decor</summary>
      <p><strong>Live</strong> — 1,618 (Operation Mindfuck Rec.), Montreal, prog tech; Biobazar, Trois-Rivières, world/trance; Delicate Frenesie, Montreal, dark psy; Florian MSK (D.M.T. Records), Montreal, minimal techno; Kola Papass, Montreal, prog/electroswing; Lynxpoint (Ghotiithout), Montreal, prog; Masingularity, Montreal, psy; MC Ultra K, Montreal, trip-hop; Monokongo, Montreal, prog; Über, Montreal, prog/tek; Wave Parasites (Hardtimes Prod), Montreal, techno; Xnorophis, Montreal, electroswing/tribal.</p>
      <p><strong>DJs</strong> — Absolute, Montreal, psy; Ajaxbeats (Konkrete Jungle / NYC Ravers), Brooklyn, jungle; Aikido (Fractal), Montreal, chill/prog; Akibel (Evolove), Montreal, psy; Akshobhya (Logic Vision Records), Montreal, min/psy; Arachnaphabob, Quebec City, psy; Audiophil, Val-David, psy/tribal; Bendala (Space Gathering), Val-David, psy/ethno; Black Cat (Hardtimes), Montreal, jungle/tek; Clectic (Les Pirateries), Montreal, eclectic; D-Brain, Montreal, psy; Deception (Studio Sundari), Montreal, psy; Der Denker (D.M.T. Records / Concepto Hipnotico), Montreal, min; Dez1 (Upsessions), Quebec City, d&amp;b; Dezz aka Serenity vs Dubldrop, Montreal, dubstep; Ed-Liner (3e œil), Montreal, techno; Elios, Montreal, chill; Exode, Montreal, downtempo; Fat Louie (Orgone Nrg Lab), Quebec City, d&amp;b/trip-hop; Floydianchild, Quebec City, shamanik dub; Galaks (I.D.J./F.A.K), Montreal, techno; Glitch (Transition Productions), Quebec City, prog/psy; Jahlex (Reggae Bash), Montreal/Jamaica, reggae; Jeff MK-Ultra (Natura Festival), Montreal, psy; Hopeku (Joof Records / Planet B.E.N.), Quebec City, prog; Horizon (24/7 Records), Montreal, psy; Karmapa, Montreal, psy; Kerston (Sound In Motion), Quebec City, dubstep; Kilura (Pounjah Familia), Quebec City, chill; Kurse, Granby, drum and bass; Lectrick and Busker (Scratch Routine), Montreal; LunarGroove (Relaxation Lounge), Montreal, chill; Mattysea (Quite Nice), Montreal, jungle, dubstep; Max Dirt, Montreal, electro; Meta B (Monkey Dub), Montreal, d&amp;b/dub; Mohinia (Logic Vision Records), Montreal, psy; Mr. Lion (Tatanka / 6'High / Quite Nice), Montreal, stepper dub; Nismo (Cyber Loft), Montreal, house; Nitrous (Monkey Dub / In Da Jungle Recording), Montreal, d&amp;b; Obsidian (Logic Vision Records), Ottawa, psydub; Okin, Montreal, tekhouse; 0m Shant1, Montreal, dubstep; Pleckobwoy (Risk / Quite Nice / 6'High), Montreal, ethno trap, jungle; Pranapapa (Tatanka / Relaxation Lounge), Quebec City, shamanik trance; Risa Selector,