    <h2 id="timeless-2014">TimeLess 2014, the first Timeless</h2>
    <p>From Friday, August 29 to Monday, September 1, 2014, for the Labour Day long weekend, L'AgorA hosted a festival that did not exist yet: the TimeLess Festival, organized by Maxime Larocque, Sumi Kim and Enakim with L'AgorA. The announcement opened like a fairy tale: "Once upon a time ॐ TimeLess… A gathering in nature that you won't forget, an experience of freedom, that will be forever part of the history of the Universe, and the land of the AgorA. You are all invited to a memorable labor day weekend. Be ready to be a part of this psychedelic phenomena."</p>
    <p>Two outdoor stages, three nights: the Neverland for psytrance and prog, the Cherry Island for chill, downtempo, minimal techno and electro swing, and the big indoor space of the bunker "in case of bad weather". On-site camping, a restaurant, "Good Vibes ☼, Leave no trace ✿, Please car pool". The headliner came from Spain: Yar Zaa, live psytrance, on Monday at 5 a.m. Tickets at Psychonaut and through PayPal: $40 until June 1, $50 until August 1, $60 until August 28, $75 at the door.</p>
    <p>After the festival, L'AgorA's page wrote: "A huge THANK YOU to the devotion of the Timeless festival promoters! Their presence made it possible for the party to unfold smoothly, and yet with such intensity!!" D-Brain, who played on Sunday: "For a last visit to L'AgorA, I had immense pleasure enjoying this mystical, high-energy place…" And a festival-goer: "Thanks to everyone for this incredible weekend! I can't wait to see you all again!" It was at Timeless, at the gate, that tickets were sold for the last Earthdance, three weeks later.</p>
    <p>This first Timeless started a twelve-year series: the festival came back on Labour Day in the following years, in Saint-Julien in 2015 (with, again, a "Neverland stage"), then elsewhere in Quebec, all the way to Sainte-Agathe-de-Lotbinière, where the 2026 edition was held.</p>
